@page "/not-found"
@layout AdminLayout

@* Reached two ways, both landing here. In-app navigation and NavigationManager.NotFound() use the
   router's NotFoundPage (the .NET 10 replacement for the deprecated <NotFound> fragment). A direct
   deep link to an unknown path dies at server-side routing with a 404; Program.cs re-executes that
   404 against this /not-found route so the styled page still renders. @layout keeps it inside the
   admin shell, the same framing the old inline LayoutView provided. *@

<PageTitle>Not found</PageTitle>

<p role="alert">Sorry, there's nothing at this address.</p>
